.TH KILIX-PONG 6 "September 2026" "kilix-pong 0.2.0" "Games Manual"
.SH NAME
kilix-pong \- luminous paddle-ball arcade game for Kitty terminals
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kilix-pong
.RI [ option ]
.br
.B kilix-pong
.RB [ --left
.IR controller ]
.RB [ --right
.IR controller ]
.RB [ --level
.IR level ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kilix-pong
is an original two-paddle arcade game rendered as a software framebuffer and
displayed directly through the Kitty graphics protocol. Each paddle can be a
human, a CPU opponent at one of three beatable levels, or a small trained
neural player; two humans play locally. Rallies gain speed, paddle position applies
english to the return angle, and the first side to 11 points wins.
.PP
Interactive play requires a Linux terminal with Kitty graphics support. Kilix
and Kitty also provide key-release events for true simultaneous local controls.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --left " controller" "\fR, \fP" --right " controller"
Play with this controller on that side:
.BR human ,
.BR cpu ,
or
.BR neural .
Overrides the remembered title-menu setup for this session.
.TP
.BI --level " level"
CPU level:
.BR easy ,
.BR normal ,
or
.BR hard .
.TP
.B --rules-test
Run targeted wall, paddle, anti-tunneling, scoring, win-state, menu, CPU, and
neural-feature checks.
.TP
.B --ai-test
Run headless tournaments: CPU levels must be ordered and beatable, and the
neural player must beat HARD from either side.
.TP
.BI --match " left right level seed games"
Play a headless tournament and print a JSON summary. A
.B human
side is driven by the built-in autopilot.
.TP
.BI --selftest " [seed] [ticks]"
Run a deterministic headless match simulation and print its state digest.
.TP
.BI --render-test " [seed] [directory]"
Write seven deterministic 960 by 540 PPM scene fixtures. The directory is
required unless
.B KILIX_PONG_RENDER_DIR
is set.
.TP
.B --asset-check
Validate runtime discovery and decoding of the production WAV bank.
.TP
.B --sound-test
Load all production sounds and play all three variants of every cue through
the first available audio sink.
.TP
.B --version
Print the program version.
.TP
.B --help
Show command and environment help.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B W, S
Move player 1 up and down.
.TP
.B Up, Down
Move player 2 in local two-player mode. With a single human, either key pair
moves that paddle. On the title screen, choose the LEFT, RIGHT or LEVEL row.
.TP
.B Left, Right
On the title screen, change the selected row.
.TP
.B Enter, Space
Start or confirm.
.TP
.B P, Escape
Pause or resume.
.TP
.B M
Toggle sound.
.TP
.B Q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/kilix-pong/settings.state
The remembered title-menu setup (both controllers, level, sound), written on
exit by the interactive game through kilix-state.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KILIX_PONG_ASSETS
Override the production asset root. The default search checks an
.I assets
directory beside the executable and then the installed
.IR ../share/kilix-pong/assets .
.TP
.B KILIX_PONG_RENDER_DIR
Default output directory for
.BR --render-test .
.TP
.B KILIX_PONG_SKIP_PROBE
When set, bypass the startup Kitty graphics capability query.
.SH AUDIO
The game loads its bundled mono 16-bit 44100 Hz WAV bank and tries
.BR pacat ,
.BR pw-play ,
.BR aplay ,
then SoX
.BR play .
If no sink opens, gameplay continues silently. All 21 WAVs are original,
deterministically generated by the included Python source.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/kilix-pong/assets/sfx/
Default installed production sound bank.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, one on runtime or validation failure, and two for invalid
command-line use.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kitty (1)
